  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2022-25 Bangladesh Rohingya and Host Communities Humanitarian Package</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Rohingya crisis is the largest and most complex humanitarian crisis in the Indo-Pacific region. As per the 2023 Response Plan (JRP) 1.52 million people need humanitarian assistance in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar, Bangladesh, including both Rohingya refugees and impacted host communities. The Bangladesh Rohingya and Host Community Humanitarian Package (2022-2025) is the country level humanitarian response to this cross border crisis originating in Myanmar and causing large-scale displacement into Bangladesh. The Bangladesh package objective is to contribute to international efforts to meet humanitarian and protection needs and increase self-reliance and resilience of Rohingya and host populations in Bangladesh. The aim is to meet refugees and host communities&#x2019; basic needs; increase their self-reliance; build resilience and social cohesion; and improve the effectiveness of the humanitarian system. The total estimated investment value is $190m over 3 years, starting in 2022-23.</narrative>
  </description>
